## Tenancy mode

**`{{ tenancy_mode }}`** (declared at bootstrap; see global CLAUDE.md `## Tenancy` for what this implies)

{% if tenancy_mode == "multi-tenant" -%}
Tenant-scoping rules apply NON-NEGOTIABLY:
- Every data-touching endpoint filters by `org_id` from JWT claims
- Every multi-tenant table has an `org_id` column with an index prefixed by it
- Cross-tenant access returns 404, not 403 (no existence disclosure)
- Apply the `isolating-multi-tenant-llm` skill for any LLM-touching code
{%- elif tenancy_mode == "single-tenant" -%}
User-level ownership checks apply NON-NEGOTIABLY:
- Every data-touching endpoint verifies `object.owner_id == current_user.id`
- NO `tenant_id` / `org_id` column on tables
- Auth + RBAC still required
{%- else -%}
No scoping rules apply. Auth is OPTIONAL. The following remain required regardless:
- Input validation at boundaries
- SSRF protection on outbound requests
- Security headers + secrets lifecycle (per global rules)
- Supply chain rules (upper-bound pinning, maintenance assessment)
{%- endif %}


## Stage

**`{{ stage }}`** (declared at bootstrap; `CONSTITUTION.md` §4, next to the global `CLAUDE.md`, lists the practices each stage switches on)

{% if stage == "explore" -%}
No real users and no real data. Leaves the stage when the first real user or real record arrives, or the code is thrown away.
{%- elif stage == "build" -%}
Real users or real data, but nobody has been promised availability. Leaves the stage when availability is promised, by a contract, a service level or a launch.
{%- elif stage == "run" -%}
Availability is promised, and the code changes actively. Leaves the stage when change is mostly fixes and upgrades.
{%- else -%}
Availability is promised, and change is mostly fixes and upgrades. Leaves the stage when it is retired or rebuilt.
{%- endif %}


Changing stage is a decision with an owner: record it here and in an ADR.

